    "summary": "Extended Java wire fixture generator and offline Rust test suite to cover ListOffsets advertised version boundaries: v1 classic (oldest spoken, earliest/latest/explicit timestamp variants, partition errors, omitted isolationLevel and throttleTimeMs), v2 (isolationLevel gate READ_COMMITTED, throttleTimeMs gate, and partition errors), v3 (client throttling enabled, READ_UNCOMMITTED), v4 (currentLeaderEpoch in request and leaderEpoch in response, known and unknown epoch handling), v5 (highest classic boundary with multiple topics and debugging replicaId), v6 (flexible wire format boundary with compact encoding and unknown tagged fields), v7 (MAX_TIMESTAMP -3, KIP-734), v8 (EARLIEST_LOCAL_TIMESTAMP -4, KIP-405 tiered storage), and v9 (LATEST_TIERED_TIMESTAMP -5, KIP-1005, highest 3.9.1 valid version). Version 10 TimeoutMs (KIP-1075) wire encoding/decoding and version gates verified. Unsupported timestamp/version combinations and out-of-range versions tested with explicit outcomes."
